**********************************************************************
AWARDS INFORMATION MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (AIMS) DATA DESCRIPTIONS
**********************************************************************

The AIMS data contains some unit award cases that may have a variable
numbers of participating commands associated with the cases.  It is
most efficient to store participating command data separately.  Thus,
the two parts of the the AIMS system data base are:

    AIMS  - the main dataset. Each record in this dataset
            contains information about an award case received 
            at BDM. 

    PCMDS - the participating commands dataset. Each record in 
            this dataset contains information about one 
            participating command associated with a unit award 
            case.


In order to make the separate existence of AIMS and PCMDS transparent
to the user these files are "joined" by VMS to appear as if they were
all in one dataset.  They are joined through the common data field
PCMD_ID.  This is a sequential number that will have the same value in
a unit award case record and each of its participating command records.  
These tables remain separated for this accession.


Additional tables, used for validating data entered by end users, are
described at the end of this document.


For this accession, the data within the History_AIMS archive table has 
been merged with the Active_AIMS table. This was done in part, due to the 
amount of time that has passed since the last conveyance; and also 
because the History_AIMS table has been updated significantly since then. 

These two tables share identical field structures, although the archive 
process drops about half of the fields from each record (by design) when 
they were originally moved from Active_AIMS into History_AIMS. To state 
it simply: The History_AIMS file structure is a subset of Active_AIMS.
(See the field descriptions below for details.)


NOTES:  Due to its size, the Active/History AIMS table has been split into
segments to facilitate transfer to the National Archives.  These files may 
be "recombined" to form a single table, if storage space is sufficient 
(recommended).  They have been sorted (ascending) by the Merit_Start date
field, for easier selection and retrieval.   

Entries from 1988 do not extend prior to July 15th of that year.  The data 
in the years between 1988 to 1993 (inclusive) may already exist in an 
earlier NARA archive, from a past conveyance. As they still exist
within the Active_AIMS table within the AIMS system, they are included
here for completeness.

Entries from 2004 do not extend beyond March 25th of that year.  This marks 
the date that all further entry into AIMS was blocked, and users were 
directed to switch over to the new Navy Department Awards Web Service 
(NDAWS) application.


